{"id": "EUVD-2026-86984", "enisaUuid": "27b9ebc8-af10-3403-94d0-d883fdb98e83", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnvme: fix racy access to FDP placement id array\n\nnvme_query_fdp_info() is called per-path and therefore prone to races.\n\nIt populates head->nr_plids/head->plids for fdp registration.\nBut nothing protects that pair from concurrent access - two paths scanning\nthe same namespace can race to populate it.\n\nAvoid the race by moving this initialization work to nvme_alloc_ns_head()\nwhich is called once per shared namespace.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:36:24", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:14:46", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e0a23e3c8c4c3ce11529fa70d2292b4e56d143ba", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/56e1c6bbe4bb084d7ecf61698afdf70be23dd35f"], "aliases": ["GHSA-r8g9-g582-fv58", "CVE-2026-98153"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.08, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "46040228-253f-3082-a85f-ed083feff4a8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.16"}, {"id": "5896fa2d-5b75-34e7-b71e-fc8c2da9be94", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "30b5f20bb2ddab013035399e5c7e6577da49320a <56e1c6bbe4bb084d7ecf61698afdf70be23dd35f"}, {"id": "8a69dbfa-3493-3967-a126-fd1606d5c7b5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "9456c624-bc7e-37d8-bf47-ebcef300ffcd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "b10abbc8-8e9e-3a8f-a9d0-672efcbb1aa3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "d0689c80-1d7d-3721-bda1-5e538b36a6d3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "30b5f20bb2ddab013035399e5c7e6577da49320a <e0a23e3c8c4c3ce11529fa70d2292b4e56d143ba"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9228c8b4-c451-3390-be2d-bbc4d21229af", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}